From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Winter <danielwinterw@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 20:12:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(skippy): keep a view's dynamic axis when it slices
 another axis

Stage-program extraction matched a view's dynamic token axis by shape. When
the view sliced a different axis whose extent equalled the captured token
count, two axes matched and extraction failed with "stage program view
requires an explicit dynamic geometry recipe".

DeepSeek2 MLA hits this on every split stage: kv_cmpr takes the first
kv_lora_rank (512) rows of the 576-wide kv_cmpr_pe, and the 512-token prefill
profile matches 512. GLM-4.7-Flash could not install its stage program on
any split stage, with or without native MTP. A view that keeps the dynamic
axis's extent and byte stride now carries that axis through unchanged.
---
 src/skippy/stage_program_extraction.cpp | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/skippy/stage_program_extraction.cpp b/src/skippy/stage_program_extraction.cpp
index 08e28da9f..28d14a023 100644
--- a/src/skippy/stage_program_extraction.cpp
+++ b/src/skippy/stage_program_extraction.cpp
@@ -254,7 +254,15 @@ bool extraction::run() {
                             const bool identity_view = tensor->view_offs == 0 &&
                                     dimensions(tensor) == dimensions(tensor->src[0]) &&
                                     byte_strides(tensor) == byte_strides(tensor->src[0]);
-                            if (identity_view) {
+                            // A view that keeps the dynamic axis's extent and byte stride
+                            // slices other axes only, so the dynamic axis carries through.
+                            // DeepSeek2 MLA reaches this case: kv_cmpr takes the first
+                            // kv_lora_rank rows of kv_cmpr_pe, and kv_lora_rank can equal
+                            // the captured token count, which makes shapes alone ambiguous.
+                            const bool keeps_dynamic_axis = source_axis < GGML_MAX_DIMS &&
+                                    tensor->ne[source_axis] == tensor->src[0]->ne[source_axis] &&
+                                    tensor->nb[source_axis] == tensor->src[0]->nb[source_axis];
+                            if (identity_view || keeps_dynamic_axis) {
                                 // Equal extents on several axes make shape-only matching ambiguous.
                                 // An identity view preserves the source dynamic axis by definition;
                                 // GLM-DSA top-k reaches this case when top_k == captured token count.
